  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (PCA n2000, single profile) achieves 0.485 accuracy while image (ResNet50, single profile) only reaches 0.208, making RNA the dominant modality by a wide margin. Uncertainty: We have no evidence yet on whether a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) can improve upon the simple PCA baseline, and this is the highest-leverage design choice since RNA drives performance. This experiment (config_004) tests scvi_n200 vs PCA n2000 with all other settings held constant (rna_only, singleprofile, no aggregation/fusion), isolating the effect of the RNA representation. It is the best next step because: (1) it is a clean single-variable comparison against config_001, (2) the RNA encoder choice will inform all subsequent multimodal experiments, and (3) with 7 experiments remaining, establishing the best RNA representation early allows informed exploitation in later multimodal and multiprofile configurations."
